From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:22:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 015/342] network: add Amlogic Meson GXBB Ethernet driver
 (meson_dwmac)

Device-manager driver for the DesignWare GMAC 3.70a of the S905
(ODROID-C2), attached through the device tree ("amlogic,meson-gxbb-dwmac"),
published as net/meson_dwmac/0:

- relies on the firmware for clocks, pin muxing, power domain, the
  Amlogic PRG_ETH0 glue (RGMII, 2 ns TX delay) and PHY reset; resets and
  programs the MAC/DMA side only
- 64+64 chained "normal" descriptors, each in its own cache line, 2 KB
  copy buffers; explicit cache maintenance (the DMA does not snoop)
- read/write hooks, DMA interrupts wake readers/writers; the handler
  clears until nothing is pending and also claims the MAC/MMC/PMT summary
  bits, and all sources are masked before it is installed (an unclaimed
  interrupt had made the kernel disable the IRQ)
- RTL8211F link polled over MDIO once a second (speed, duplex)
- pass-all-multicast filter, promiscuous mode, link state reporting

Tested on the ODROID-C2: DHCP, 1000 Mbit/s full duplex, ping both ways
(~1.3 ms), 2 x 10000-packet flood pings without loss, 100 MB FTP round
trip with matching sha256 (30.5 MB/s up incl. eMMC write, 18.8 MB/s down).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
